    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0122" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/747: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-08T10:00:00-03:00">December 8, 1941—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>517. Department’s circular telegram December 7, 6 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >10 p.m.?</hi>] Oral communication regarding Japanese aggression has been
                    communicated to Guani<anchor n="63" xml:id="d138-f1"/> who will give me the
                    requested expression of the views of the Uruguayan Government somewhat later.
                    For the time being he asked me to advise the Department that Uruguay considers
                    itself already solidly with the United States and is consulting other
                    governments with a view to making this solidarity effective throughout the
                    continent. He mentioned in particular consultation with Brazil and
                    Argentina.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d138-f1" n="63" xml:id="d138-f1-content">
                <p>Alberto Guani, Uruguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
